Page parser improvements:
```python
def parse_page(body):
    head = body[:200000].decode('utf-8','replace')
    def meta(name):
        m = re.search(rf'<meta[^>]+name="{re.escape(name)}"[^>]+content="([^"]*)"', head, re.I) or \
            re.search(rf'<meta[^>]+content="([^"]*)"[^>]+name="{re.escape(name)}"', head, re.I)
        return html.unescape(m.group(1)).strip() if m else ''
    title = meta('citation_title') or (regex <title>)
    authors = '; '.join(re.findall(r'<meta[^>]+name="citation_author"[^>]+content="([^"]*)"', head, re.I))
    date = meta('citation_date') or meta('citation_online_date')
    year = int(date[:4]) if re.match(r'\d{4}', date) else None
    abstract = meta('citation_abstract')
    journal = meta('citation_journal_title')
    doi = meta('citation_doi')
    versions = [ (int(y), full) for y,full in re.findall(r'\[v(\d+)\][^<]*?(\d{4})', ...) ]
```
Version history: `[v2] Fri, 22 Feb 2019 03:51:20 UTC` → find all `\[v\d+\][^<]{0,80}?(\d{4})` over the page text. Collect years as `version_years`.
Journal reference line: `Journal reference:\s*([^<]{5,200})` → journal_ref.

Year collection: for each source: explicit `year`, plus `version_years` (list), plus if `journal_ref` contains a 4-digit year, include it. year_ok if any candidate year within 1 of ledger year. year_ok False only if candidates exist and none consistent. That handles 057 (version year 2019) and 053 (journal ref 2025; crossref 2025).

Excerpt matching sources: only sources with title sim ≥ 0.5 count; haystack from their abstract + title + authors + venue + journal_ref + doi + version strings.

